  "sourceTitle": "Horseradish Dip",
  "sourceText": "Horseradish Dip\nBy: Cresent\nPublished: Friday, February 12, 2010 - 2:37pm\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n1 cup cottage cheese\n2 tablespoons prepared horseradish\n2 tablespoons finely-chopped green pepper\nteaspoon dried basil\nteaspoon crushed dried marjoram\nteaspoon salt\n1 dsh cayenne pepper\n\nPreparation\n\n1 Combine all ingredients, mix well, and chill at least 2 hours before serving. 2 Serve as a dip for raw vegetables or cooked ham cubes on toothpicks. 3 This recipe yields 1 1/4 cups.",
  "parsedSource": {
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "sourceText": "1 cup cottage cheese"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "2 tablespoons prepared horseradish"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "2 tablespoons finely-chopped green pepper"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "teaspoon dried basil"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "teaspoon crushed dried marjoram"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "teaspoon salt"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "1 dsh cayenne pepper"
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "1 Combine all ingredients, mix well, and chill at least 2 hours before serving. 2 Serve as a dip for raw vegetables or cooked ham cubes on toothpicks. 3 This recipe yields 1 1/4 cups."
      }
    ]
